AWS Services Used

Amazon VPC — Provides isolated networking for the application.
Amazon EC2 — Hosts the Apache web servers.
Application Load Balancer — Distributes incoming traffic across EC2 instances.
Auto Scaling Group — Automatically maintains the desired number of EC2 instances.
Elastic Load Balancing Health Checks — Detects unhealthy instances.
Security Groups — Controls inbound and outbound traffic.

High Availability Features

EC2 instances deployed across multiple Availability Zones.
Application Load Balancer distributes traffic between instances.
Auto Scaling Group maintains the desired number of healthy instances.
Target group health checks monitor instance availability.
Failed instances can be automatically replaced.

Automation

#!/bin/bash
yum update -y
yum install -y httpd
systemctl start httpd
systemctl enable httpd
echo "<h1>Hello World from $(hostname -f)</h1>" > /var/www/html/index.html

This script automatically installs and configures Apache when new instances launch.
